lls need atp but they don't  make glucose how do animal cells get  glucose well we get glucose from the  outside  by consuming food the food that we eat  has glucose in it the glucose is  digested and eventually makes its way  into our cells where it's absorbed into  the mitochondria the mitochondria of our  animal cells can then create atp and  like the notes say atp is the energy  used by cells it provides the power that  cells need to do their work so i hope  this nice little connection here between  photosynthesis and cellular respiration  has been helpful thanks for watching


